SAR ADC dynamic comparator on PSP103, real device charges, 50 C: the VACASK twin of sar_cmp_psp_real.cir
// specs/analog/decks/vacask_cmp_real.sim -- second-simulator data for specs/analog/vacask_compare.t27 (analog, #10911, epic #10486).
// A netlist in VACASK's own syntax plus a control block; the numbers are read from its raw files (see "What is read").
// Circuits, side by side in one netlist, as in sar_cmp_psp_real.cir (the ngspice deck this one repeats, element for element):
//   xb    the subcircuit dynamic_comparator with 4 fF on dp and dn (bdp, bdn): the latch alone;
//   xtop  the subcircuit dynamic_comparator_top: the same latch, 4 fF on each output, an inverter on each, 4 fF on each inverter output
//         and the NAND of the two inverter outputs, "Valid". The converter's comparator with the loads it has there.
// The subcircuits are the golden SAR deck's (uberWAVE wp2-parser/golden/top.spice, GPL-2.0). They are fetched at run time and NEVER vendored:
// the file vacask_golden.inc is made from the very subcircuit text that SAR_GOLDEN_SUBCKTS names for the ngspice decks, by one awk program that
// changes only the syntax and stops with an error line on any line it does not know:
//   .subckt NAME p1 p2 ..          ->  subckt NAME (p1 p2 ..)          .ends  ->  ends
//   XMk d g s b MASTER params..    ->  XMk (d g s b) MASTER params..   (MASTER = sg13_lv_nmos or sg13_lv_pmos; w, l, ng, m unchanged)
//   xk n1 n2 .. SUBCKT             ->  xk (n1 n2 ..) SUBCKT
//   Ck n1 n2 VALUE m=1             ->  Ck (n1 n2) cap c=VALUE
//   * comment lines are dropped. Only dynamic_comparator, dynamic_comparator_top, inverter and nand are taken.
// PSP103 (IHP-Open-PDK 21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40, cornerMOSlv mos_tt) through OSDI, 50 C, with ALL its charge: the gate, overlap
// and junction capacitance of every device. Nothing is scaled; an ideal 1.6 ps clock stands for the delay-cell clkc; the inputs are held.
// THE MODELS are the PDK's own, converted to VACASK's syntax by VACASK's converter (python3 -m vacask.sg13g2tovc from VACASK's source tree,
// PDK_ROOT a COPY of the checkout because the converter writes into it): sg13g2_vacask_common.lib and cornerMOSlv.lib in libs.tech/vacask/models of
// the copy, and the instance wrappers sg13_lv_nmos and sg13_lv_pmos of the PDK's own sg13g2_moslv_mod.lib, with its formulas for as, ad, ps, pd.
// THE OSDI FILE is psp103.osdi, the one the ngspice decks load: the ngspice image's /opt/osdi directory is first on module_path_prefix in a
// .vacaskrc.toml next to the deck, so both simulators run the SAME compiled model file. (The converter compiles its own copy, which differs in bytes.)
// Run: PDK_ROOT=<converted copy> PDK=ihp-sg13g2 vacask -sp vacask_cmp_real.sim    (cwd holds vacask_golden.inc and the .vacaskrc.toml)
// INPUTS: VDD 1.5 V, common mode 0.75 V. The swept variable sd is the signed half input in units of 2^-24 V: VDP = 0.75 + sd h, VDN = 0.75 - sd h,
// so VDP - VDN = 2 sd units. Write sd and the 16777216 as REALS: an integer sd divides to 0.
//   sweep hs (analysis run1)   sd = +-16777, +-4194, +-1049, +-262, +-84, +-8, +-1: the ngspice deck's first list.
//   sweep ds (analysis scan)   VDP - VDN = d units for d = -2700, -2600, -2571, -2570, -2540, -2400 (sd = d / 2): its second list.
//   sweep fs (analysis fine)   d = -2598, -2594, -2590, -2586, -2582, -2578, -2574, -2572, around VACASK's own flip point of xtop.
// The clock is 0 until 200 ps, then rises over 1.6 ps (its 50 % point at 200.8 ps).
// THE START: icmode "uic" and the spec's rest (ap = an = net2 = net3 = n_clkc = 1.5 V, dp = dn = 0, net1 = 0.4009999632835388 V) and the
// inverters' and NAND's outputs at their logic values; nodes not named start at 0 and settle in the 200 ps before the clock (the ngspice deck's
// .ic with uic). Both simulators leave this start the same way: vdd, vdp, vdn and clkc are not in the list either and start at 0 V, the state is
// not a solution, and the outputs jump from 0 to about 1.2 V in the first 0.05 ps, then fall back through 0.75 V at about 150 ps, before the clock.
// Their pre-clock waveforms agree within 0.4 mV from 1 ps on and within 0.15 mV from 30 ps on (specs/analog/vacask_compare.t27).
// INTEGRATION: trapezoidal (VACASK's default, tran_method), the step capped at 0.5 ps, reltol 1e-8, vntol 1e-11, abstol 1e-13 as in the ngspice deck.
// WHAT IS READ (outside this file, from run1.raw, scan.raw and fine.raw): tck, the clock through 0.75 V; tfirst, the first of dp and dn of xb
// through 0.75 V rising at or after tck (the early rise of the start is not a decision; the ngspice deck's meas does not see it either); tres,
// |dp - dn| of xb through 0.75 V; tvalid, Valid through 0.75 V rising after tck; xb's dp and dn and xtop's dp and dn at 3 ns. Crossings are linear
// interpolations between consecutive output points, as ngspice's meas does; times are given after tck.

include "sg13g2_vacask_common.lib"
include "cornerMOSlv.lib" section=mos_tt
include "vacask_golden.inc"

load "capacitor.osdi"
model v vsource
model cap capacitor

vdd (vdd 0) v dc=1.5
vdp (vdp 0) v dc=0.75+sd/16777216.0
vdn (vdn 0) v dc=0.75-sd/16777216.0
vclk (clkc 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0, 200p, 0, 201.6p, 1.5]
xb (vdp vdn clkc vdd 0 bdp bdn) dynamic_comparator
cbdp (bdp 0) cap c=4f
cbdn (bdn 0) cap c=4f
xtop (vocp vocn valid vdp vdn clkc vdd 0) dynamic_comparator_top

control
  var sd=0
  options temp=50 reltol=1e-8 vntol=1e-11 abstol=1e-13
  save v(clkc) v(bdp) v(bdn) v(valid) v('xtop:dp') v('xtop:dn')
  var ic0={"xb:ap", 1.5, "xb:an", 1.5, "xb:net1", 0.4009999632835388, "xb:net2", 1.5, "xb:net3", 1.5, "bdp", 0, "bdn", 0, "xb:n_clkc", 1.5,
    "xtop:x1:ap", 1.5, "xtop:x1:an", 1.5, "xtop:x1:net1", 0.4009999632835388, "xtop:x1:net2", 1.5, "xtop:x1:net3", 1.5, "xtop:dp", 0, "xtop:dn", 0,
    "xtop:x1:n_clkc", 1.5, "vocp", 1.5, "vocn", 1.5, "valid", 0}
  sweep hs variable="sd" values=[16777, -16777, 4194, -4194, 1049, -1049, 262, -262, 84, -84, 8, -8, 1, -1] continuation=0
    analysis run1 tran step=0.1p stop=3n maxstep=0.5p icmode="uic" ic=ic0
  sweep ds variable="sd" values=[-1350, -1300, -1285.5, -1285, -1270, -1200] continuation=0
    analysis scan tran step=0.1p stop=3n maxstep=0.5p icmode="uic" ic=ic0
  sweep fs variable="sd" values=[-1299.0, -1297.0, -1295.0, -1293.0, -1291.0, -1289.0, -1287.0, -1286.0] continuation=0
    analysis fine tran step=0.1p stop=3n maxstep=0.5p icmode="uic" ic=ic0
endc
